+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bring-up
========

The package installs the CGI program at
${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www/cgi-bin/fuguoracle, the key generator at
${PREFIX}/sbin/fuguoracle-keygen, and the rc.d script ${RCDIR}/fuguoracle.
The script runs a dedicated slowcgi(8) inside the ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www
chroot, as the user _fuguoracle.

1. Add the server block of ${PREFIX}/share/examples/fuguoracle/httpd.conf
   to ${SYSCONFDIR}/httpd.conf. Put the host name of the service in place of
   oracle.example.org. acme-client(1) supplies the certificate and the
   key at the two paths of the block.

2. Make the static key, and note the public key that the program prints:

   # fuguoracle-keygen

3. Enable and start the services:

   # rcctl enable httpd fuguoracle
   # rcctl start fuguoracle httpd

The service needs no cron job and no cleanup task. Monitor the free space
of the filesystem that holds ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www/fuguoracle/pins: any
caller can create a record. A dedicated filesystem on
${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www/fuguoracle keeps a fill away from the rest of
${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www.

Backup
======

The static key is the service. A loss of
${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www/fuguoracle/private.key, or of the pins directory,
makes the PIN unlock of every enrolled client permanently inoperable.
Back up the key offline at enrollment time, and treat the pins directory
as precious.

Restore the pins directory only after an incident review. A restore
rewinds the attempt counter and the replay counter of each record to the
backup time.

Key rotation
============

A rotation in place is not supported: every storage key derives from the
static key, so a new key orphans every record. On a suspected key
compromise:

1. Stop the service, and clear the key and the records:

   # rcctl stop fuguoracle
   # rm ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www/fuguoracle/private.key
   # rm ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/www/fuguoracle/pins/*

2. Make a new key:

   # fuguoracle-keygen

3. Start the service. Provision the new public key into every client,
   and have every client run set_pin again.

Client provisioning
===================

Each client needs the oracle URL and the static public key. fuguoracle(8)
states the provisioning rules: the URL form, the TLS position, a private
CA, and a second URL.

Blockstream Jade
================

Provision a Jade with the companion app, or with the gdk call
update_pinserver: set the oracle URL and the static public key. An
initialized Jade refuses a change of the oracle public key, with the
message "Cannot update initialized unit". Provision the oracle before the
first seed setup, or factory-reset the unit first. A URL update and a
certificate update stay possible on an initialized unit.

Live test
=========

Before any real use, provision a spare reference client against the
oracle, and pass a full cycle: set the PIN, unlock, and the three-strike
wipe. Record the date of the pass.
